<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soissons</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Augusta Suessionum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soissons is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aisne">Aisne</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As Augusta Suessionum it was the Roman centre of the Suessiones, and in 486 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a>, ruler of the Domain of Soissons, near the city. It then served as a capital of Frankish kings, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> was proclaimed king there in 751.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soissons.jpg" alt="Soissons" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soissons-hotel-de-ville.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
